1
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:03,431
(Q1) Good evening. King's Restaurant.

2
00:00:03,431 --> 00:00:08,004
Good evening. I'm ringing about the job I understand you have vacant.

3
00:00:08,004 --> 00:00:08,995
Oh yes.

4
00:00:08,995 --> 00:00:11,882
I'd like to find out a few more details, if I may.

5
00:00:11,882 --> 00:00:13,868
Yes, of course. Can I take your name?

6
00:00:13,868 --> 00:00:15,899
It's Peter Chin.

7
00:00:15,899 --> 00:00:25,128
Okay Peter. Well, if you want to ask about the job and then if we're both still interested, we could arrange for you to come for an interview.

8
00:00:25,128 --> 00:00:31,046
Great, thanks. I'm afraid I missed the advert for the job but heard about it from a friend.

9
00:00:31,046 --> 00:00:33,699
That's no problem at all. What would you like to know?

10
00:00:33,699 --> 00:00:38,076
[🟢 定位] Well, um, what sort of work is it - washing up?

11
00:00:38,076 --> 00:00:40,097
[Q1答案句] It's answering the phone.

12
00:00:40,097 --> 00:00:42,719
Oh right, fine.

13
00:00:42,719 --> 00:00:45,244
And not waiting at table.

14
00:00:45,244 --> 00:00:49,548
(Q2) That'd be good. And how many nights a week would it be?

15
00:00:49,548 --> 00:00:52,559
Well, we're really only busy at the weekend.

16
00:00:52,559 --> 00:00:54,092
So two nights?

17
00:00:54,092 --> 00:00:57,942
Three actually, so it would work out at twelve hours a week.

18
00:00:57,942 --> 00:01:01,413
That'd be fine. It wouldn't interfere with my studies.

19
00:01:01,413 --> 00:01:02,875
Are you at the university?

20
00:01:02,875 --> 00:01:05,208
Yes. First year Physics student.

21
00:01:05,208 --> 00:01:06,141
Oh, right.

22
00:01:06,141 --> 00:01:11,621
Um, and because I'm not an EU national would I need a work permit?

23
00:01:11,621 --> 00:01:14,622
Yes you would. Just get your tutor to sign it.

24
00:01:14,622 --> 00:01:21,125
That wouldn't be a problem, if I were to get the job. Um, where exactly is the restaurant?

25
00:01:21,125 --> 00:01:27,227
Well, we have two branches - the one we're recruiting for is in Hillsdunne Road.

26
00:01:27,227 --> 00:01:30,997
I don't know that. How do you spell it please?

27
00:01:30,997 --> 00:01:38,338
[Q2答案句] It's H-I-double L-S-D-U-double N-E Road.

28
00:01:38,338 --> 00:01:42,420
(Q3) Got that. Thanks. Is it near a bus stop?

29
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:46,107
[Q3答案句] Yes. The nearest one would probably be just beside the Library.

30
00:01:46,107 --> 00:01:52,234
(Q4) Oh yes, I know it. That'd be fine for me. And could I ask about the pay?

31
00:01:52,234 --> 00:01:55,363
[Q4答案句] We're offering £4.45 an hour.

32
00:01:55,363 --> 00:02:02,136
That's very good. My last job was £3.95 an hour.

33
00:02:02,136 --> 00:02:06,153
(Q5) We feel it's pretty good and we also offer some good fringe benefits.

34
00:02:06,153 --> 00:02:06,942
Really?

35
00:02:06,942 --> 00:02:10,201
Well, we give you a free dinner, so you eat well.

36
00:02:10,201 --> 00:02:12,707
Right, better than hostel food!

37
00:02:12,707 --> 00:02:18,344
[Q5答案句] We certainly hope so! And we also offer extra pay for working on national holidays.

38
00:02:18,344 --> 00:02:20,293
(Q6) Oh, that's a really good perk, isn't it?

39
00:02:20,293 --> 00:02:28,053
[Q6答案句] Yes, we think so. And then because of the difficulties of getting public transport, if you're working after 11 o'clock we drive you home.

40
00:02:28,053 --> 00:02:29,628
Oh, that's good to know.

41
00:02:29,628 --> 00:02:35,003
(Q7) Well, we'd certainly be interested in inviting you for an interview, if you're still interested?

42
00:02:35,003 --> 00:02:41,008
Oh yes, certainly. Could I just also ask what qualities you're looking for?

43
00:02:41,008 --> 00:02:48,424
[Q7答案句] Well, for this particular job we want a clear voice, which you obviously do have!

44
00:02:48,424 --> 00:02:49,640
Thanks.

45
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:52,970
(Q8) [Q8答案句] And you must be able to think quickly, you know.

46
00:02:52,970 --> 00:02:54,629
Well, I hope I'd.

47
00:02:54,629 --> 00:02:59,328
(Q9) So, when could you come in for an interview? We're actually quite quiet tonight?

48
00:02:59,328 --> 00:03:07,975
[Q9答案句] Sorry, I couldn't come tonight. Or tomorrow, I'm afraid. Thursday's okay - that'd be 22nd of October.

49
00:03:07,975 --> 00:03:09,758
Fine, after 5 p.m.?

50
00:03:09,758 --> 00:03:12,960
Yes, fine. Would 6 o'clock be okay?

51
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:17,191
(Q10) Perfect. And could you bring along with the names of two referees?

52
00:03:17,191 --> 00:03:18,913
Yes, that's fine, no problem.

53
00:03:18,913 --> 00:03:21,259
Good, I look forward to seeing you.

54
00:03:21,259 --> 00:03:24,815
Oh, by the way, who should I ask for?

55
00:03:24,815 --> 00:03:28,385
Oh yes, of course, sorry. My name is Samira Manuja.

56
00:03:28,385 --> 00:03:30,903
Can you spell that, please?

57
00:03:30,903 --> 00:03:35,414
[Q10答案句] M-A-N-U-J-A.&nbsp;&nbsp;

58
00:03:35,414 --> 00:03:38,997
Okay, I've got that. Thanks very much.

59
00:03:38,997 --> 00:03:41,497
Look forward to seeing you…

